    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d361">

                <pb facs="0651" n="519" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg519"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/2802: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Jay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-12-15T13:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 15,
                                1926—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 4:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>98. My No. 96, December 9, 8 p.m. Minister Gallardo informed me that he
                    communicated to the President, when the latter returned after <pb facs="0652"
                        n="520" xml:id="pg520"/> brief absence from the city, the Brazilian
                    Government’s reply which expresses the opinion that intervention at Lima is
                    inopportune at present moment for reasons that have already been explained to
                    Morgan. Although Argentina does not contemplate any immediate action, Mr.
                    Gallardo thinks that delay of Government of Peru in replying to your memorandum
                    is a favorable sign.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
